# Abeesa — Restaurant Ordering Platform

**Live Demo:** _[Add your Render URL here once deployed]_

## Description

Abeesa is a multi-restaurant food ordering platform built with Django. Restaurant
owners can list their restaurant, manage their menu, and track incoming orders.
Customers can browse restaurants, place orders with delivery details, confirm
payment via bank transfer, message restaurants directly, and track their order
status in real time. Built as the final project for the Dune Cohort Backend
Development with Python & Django course.

## Features

- User registration, login, and logout (Django auth)
- Restaurant owners can create, edit, and delete their own menu items (full CRUD, owner-only permissions)
- Customers can browse all restaurants and view individual restaurant menus
- Customers can place orders with delivery address and contact phone
- Session-based cart-free ordering (quantities selected directly on the order form)
- Order status tracking: Pending → Confirmed → Preparing → Completed (or Cancelled)
- Customers can cancel their own pending/confirmed orders
- Restaurant owners can view all incoming orders and update order status (owner-only, restricted action)
- Manual bank-transfer payment flow: customer marks "I've Paid," owner confirms receipt
- Restaurant-specific contact messaging with canned-reply system
- General site-wide contact form
- Fully responsive design (mobile, tablet, desktop) with a hamburger nav on small screens
- Scroll-triggered fade-in animations
- REST API (Django REST Framework) for menu items and orders, with authentication-protected write operations
- Custom-designed UI with Google Fonts (Poppins/Inter), custom CSS, hero image, and brand logo

## Tech Stack

- Python 3.14
- Django 6.0
- Django REST Framework
- SQLite (development) / PostgreSQL (production)
- HTML5, CSS3 (custom, no framework), vanilla JavaScript
- WhiteNoise (static file serving in production)
- Render (deployment)

